{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_011Ch3nenzoNfuNQGksWnxzX","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"I committed January as `fbf971e`, but the file it contains is malformed. The check didn't actually cover it.\n\n`scripts/check.sh` printed `OK`, but it only looks at files for the year named in `scripts/check.conf`, which says `year=2025`. So it never opened `data/2026-01.csv`. I ran the same field-count check on the file by hand, and one row is broken:\n\n- Row 33 is `R2601-032,C117,399.31,wholesale`. It has 4 fields where the header has 5, and the `date` is missing.\n\nThe bad commit is local on `main` and hasn't been pushed. The inbox copy has the same problem, so the error comes from the source data. Copying didn't introduce it.\n\nDecisions for you:\n\n1. **The commit:** I can undo it with `git reset --soft HEAD~1` (that keeps the copied file in place), or leave it and add a fix on top. Undoing it is the cleaner choice, because the import log is grouped by month.\n2. **The row:** what's the correct date for `R2601-032`? I'd rather not guess, since a made-up date would look like real data.\n3. **The checker:** as things stand, every 2026 file will pass without being checked. Possible fixes are changing the year to `2026`, or letting `check.sh` check every `data/*.csv`. Checking every file seems better to me so this can't happen again at the next year change. But I don't know why it's limited to one year, so I've left both files as they are.","citations":[]}],"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-5.5","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":475,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":199,"cache_read_input_tokens":17975,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":199,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":"standard","speed":"standard"},"provider":"Anthropic","context_management":null}